# Line endings.
#
# The conformance suite compares a fixture's output against its `.out`
# file byte for byte. Without a rule here, git rewrites LF to CRLF when
# checking out on Windows, so every golden-output test fails on a line
# ending that was never in the repository. No fixture contains a
# carriage return on purpose, so LF everywhere is safe as well as
# correct.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises on commit and checks out with LF on
# every platform, Windows included.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Images the book renders, which must not be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.avif binary
*.qoi binary

# Inert until Zuri is accepted into github-linguist.
#
# The attribute is `linguist-language`, not `language`, and its value is
# looked up in Linguist's own `languages.yml`. A name that is not in
# that file is ignored, so there is no way to force `.zu` to show as
# Zuri from here: the name has to exist upstream first. Written in the
# correct form so it starts working the day it does.
*.zu linguist-language=Zuri linguist-detectable=true

